WHY THE CARVE-OUT

The App Store's terms impose usage restrictions that the GPL family of licences
forbids a distributor from adding; the two have been understood to conflict at
least since VLC was pulled from the store in 2011. Keeping `ios/` outside the
AGPL is what lets the same code be published here and shipped through
TestFlight and the App Store.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of the
files in this directory to:

  a. read, study and quote from them, including in commentary and teaching;
  b. build them and run the result on devices you own or control, for your own
     personal, non-commercial use, including against your own Meals server; and
  c. modify them and submit those modifications back to this project.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

  d. redistribute these files or any derivative of them, in source or compiled
     form, to anyone else;
  e. publish an application derived from them to the App Store or any other
     application marketplace; or
  f. use them, or any derivative, for a commercial purpose.

CONTRIBUTIONS

Because this app is distributed through the App Store, contributions to `ios/`
can only be accepted from contributors who have signed the contributor licence
agreement described in ../CONTRIBUTING.md. A contribution under the AGPL, or
under any licence obliging the copyright holder to grant rights Apple's terms
do not permit, cannot be merged here.

